# One construction lifecycle on an ordinary founded settlement: the production founding
# transaction, a bounded wait for the founder to have dedicated a stockpile, a startup census of
# what the settlement actually holds, the production quote/CanPay/commission with its physical
# timber and water debit, real engine turns spent by the bounded advance verb, and the completion
# of that exact job into a functional building, followed by a real save a separate cold-load
# profile can be imported from.
#
# RENAMED from lifecycle-stockpile-native-check (ZAP-034 root ruling): this is the
# founding-first-city ROAD, which the Quickstart road (see
# lifecycle-stockpile-native-check.persona) makes obsolete as a way to prove the construction
# lifecycle -- this file's job now is to document its own honest, bounded refusal.
#
# BOUNDED WAIT FOR DEDICATION. `realize` places no camp kit and dedicates nothing --
# dedicating a stockpile is a founder-interactive act (Core/KingdomCharterPart.Vessels.cs,
# Growth/KingdomMaterials.05.StockpileAndPaymentGates.cs) a sealed script never drives, so
# lifecycle-open no longer refuses the instant realize finishes. Each attempt spends one ordinary
# 100-turn `advance` and journals its reading as an OK "still waiting" row
# (KingdomQuickstartLifecycleOpenWait); this repeats up to
# KingdomQuickstartLifecycleOpenWait.MaxChunks times before an honest refusal names the last
# reading. On this profile the predicate never becomes true (dedication has no automatic
# production path), so this script is expected to end in that honest, bounded refusal rather than
# reaching lifecycle-build -- proof that the wait was genuinely exhausted, not skipped, and a
# clear signal for the next ticket (an interactive-dedication scenario verb, or an automatic
# camp-kit dedication) rather than a same-turn false alarm.
#
# Nothing is fabricated: no stock is minted and no job is forced into a phase. The settlement
# pays out of its own accumulated stores, so lifecycle-build refuses honestly when the economy
# has not yet paid for the design, and lifecycle-grown refuses when the turn budget expires
# before the building stands. Every refusal here is the point of the persona, not a failure of it.
#
# The cold-load session and the next action after it are NOT in this script: they need a second
# profile imported from this save. Tools/check-quickstart-lifecycle.py reports them as BLOCKER
# until that leg exists, and never as a pass.
DESCRIPTION=documented refusal: founding-first-city has no automatic stockpile dedication, so lifecycle-open waits its bounded budget then honestly refuses
REQUEST=founding-first-city
START=8.22@40,12
SCRIPT=stagedigest;realize;lifecycle-open;advance 100;lifecycle-open;advance 100;lifecycle-open;advance 100;lifecycle-open;advance 100;lifecycle-open;advance 100;lifecycle-open;lifecycle-build;advance 2400;lifecycle-grown;lifecycle-save;stagedigest
VERBS=lifecycle-open,lifecycle-build,lifecycle-grown,lifecycle-save
EXPECT=stagedigest:OK~founded=false,realize:OK,lifecycle-open:OK~step=open-wait,advance:OK,lifecycle-open:OK~step=open-wait,advance:OK,lifecycle-open:OK~step=open-wait,advance:OK,lifecycle-open:OK~step=open-wait,advance:OK,lifecycle-open:OK~step=open-wait,advance:OK,lifecycle-open:REFUSED~no dedicated stockpile appeared within 500 ordinary engine turns,STOPPED
SET=growth,construction,native-regression
TIMEOUT=1200
